1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,549
This walkthrough presents Lanka Dispatch, the Applied Machine Learning prototype prepared for Sandaru

2
00:00:05,549 --> 00:00:11,099
Rashmika, index number two six nine one eight two L. It forecasts the next local day of recorded

3
00:00:11,099 --> 00:00:16,648
electricity dispatch energy in Sri Lanka. The source is the Sri Lankan raw subset of a versioned public

4
00:00:16,648 --> 00:00:22,197
dataset compiled from PUCSL records. The daily target was rebuilt from raw readings after detecting

5
00:00:22,197 --> 00:00:27,746
duplicate plant and timestamp records and a missing interval conversion in the published daily file. This

6
00:00:27,746 --> 00:00:33,296
is a historical research tool, with no connection to live grid operations.

7
00:00:34,875 --> 00:00:40,200
In the Forecast Lab, select the day to predict and load its recorded inputs. The six editable values

8
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:45,525
describe earlier demand: one, two, seven and fourteen day lags, and the previous week's mean and

9
00:00:45,525 --> 00:00:50,851
variability. Calendar coordinates come from the selected date. For fifteen January twenty twenty five,

10
00:00:50,851 --> 00:00:56,176
the trained Gaussian process predicts about forty two point three three gigawatt hours. Its nominal

11
00:00:56,176 --> 00:01:01,501
ninety five percent observation interval runs from thirty seven point four three to forty seven point two

12
00:01:01,501 --> 00:01:06,826
three. The historical observed outcome is displayed separately. The interface calls the saved Python

13
00:01:06,826 --> 00:01:12,152
model, rather than a mock formula.

14
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:19,355
Next, change only the previous day's energy to forty two gigawatt hours and generate another forecast.

15
00:01:19,355 --> 00:01:24,960
The estimate rises to about forty four point two two gigawatt hours. The badge identifies hypothetical

16
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:30,565
inputs, while the recorded outcome stays unchanged. Below the estimate, three bars show separate group

17
00:01:30,565 --> 00:01:36,170
replacement sensitivities against a representative training day. They describe changes in this fitted

18
00:01:36,170 --> 00:01:41,775
model's output. They do not add up to the prediction and they do not prove causal effects. Internally

19
00:01:41,775 --> 00:01:47,380
consistent historical inputs remain preferable to arbitrary scenarios.

20
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,474
The interface also checks input validity. Entering a negative energy value produces an error instead of

21
00:01:54,474 --> 00:01:59,948
accepting a new prediction. The prediction panel is explicitly labelled as the last valid estimate. The

22
00:01:59,948 --> 00:02:05,421
backend independently rejects negative, oversized and non finite values. Dates outside the evaluated

23
00:02:05,421 --> 00:02:10,895
historical period receive a warning because no live data feed is available.

24
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:18,131
The evaluation tab reports the same saved experimental results as the report. Three chronological

25
00:02:18,131 --> 00:02:23,761
validation windows selected hyperparameters before the ninety seven day test. Gaussian process regression

26
00:02:23,761 --> 00:02:29,392
achieves a mean absolute error of one point five nine nine gigawatt hours, improving the weekly naive

27
00:02:29,392 --> 00:02:35,023
baseline by twenty nine point seven percent. It does not win every comparison: support vector regression

28
00:02:35,023 --> 00:02:40,653
has the lowest test mean absolute error, and random forest has the lowest root mean squared error. The

29
00:02:40,653 --> 00:02:46,284
global explanation shows greatest reliance on demand history and weekly calendar. Nominal ninety five

30
00:02:46,284 --> 00:02:51,914
percent intervals cover ninety two point eight percent of test outcomes.

31
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:59,225
Finally, replay four February twenty twenty five, Independence Day. The model forecasts about forty four

32
00:02:59,225 --> 00:03:04,951
point three seven gigawatt hours, while recorded dispatch is only thirty three point seven four. Several

33
00:03:04,951 --> 00:03:10,676
large errors coincide with verified Sri Lankan holidays omitted from the frozen predictors. That

34
00:03:10,676 --> 00:03:16,401
association suggests a future improvement, but adding holiday features now would require a fresh holdout.

35
00:03:16,401 --> 00:03:22,127
Recorded dispatch is also a coverage limited proxy for demand. The source package includes data

36
00:03:22,127 --> 00:03:27,852
provenance, code, executed notebook, model artefacts, explanations and independent checks. This video

37
00:03:27,852 --> 00:03:33,577
uses genuine interface captures with panning and synthesized narration. Student review and an accurate

38
00:03:33,577 --> 00:03:39,303
assistance disclosure remain part of submission.
